02:07:00.360 --> 02:07:03.900
mentioned, that except for those items, because we'll address those in the public

02:07:04.400 --> 02:07:07.280
hearing. I addressed— I was just waiting to see, make sure. So I apologize,

02:07:07.780 --> 02:07:10.400
mine is actually for that. I apologize. Then we'll call you up in just a

02:07:10.900 --> 02:07:12.921
few minutes when we get to that item. I understood The exact opposite. That's my

02:07:13.421 --> 02:07:16.731
dad. Thank you. My apologies. And I thought that there was 2 things

02:07:16.844 --> 02:07:19.734
he wanted to speak about. We're glad you came and you want to make public

02:07:20.234 --> 02:07:22.883
comment, and we want to hear from you. So at the appropriate time, the mayor

02:07:23.383 --> 02:07:25.225
will make sure, and Lacey will make sure you get the invite.

02:07:27.908 --> 02:07:30.408
Great. Okay. Uh, Greg Hunsaker.

02:07:38.811 --> 02:07:42.847
Hello. Hello. I moved in probably

02:07:43.347 --> 02:07:47.174
3 months ago, and I've

02:07:47.207 --> 02:07:50.862
been— I work for the Alpine School District as a bus driver,

02:07:51.916 --> 02:07:56.682
and it's just

02:07:57.182 --> 02:08:01.061
been moving in when I can, you know. And I

02:08:01.255 --> 02:08:05.230
went on an activity trip on the 4th at

02:08:05.278 --> 02:08:08.918
St. George with Pleasant Grove High School, their band.

02:08:09.383 --> 02:08:12.045
Came back Sunday the 8th,

02:08:12.895 --> 02:08:16.374
and Monday I had 2 trailers that

02:08:16.874 --> 02:08:21.073
I've been using to move, and they

02:08:21.573 --> 02:08:25.338
were tagged the day I left, and they were gone the day I got

02:08:25.838 --> 02:08:28.096
back on Monday. And, uh,

02:08:29.571 --> 02:08:32.868
and I just want to make you aware Of what's going on because—

02:08:33.211 --> 02:08:34.371
I'm sorry.

02:08:41.424 --> 02:08:44.774
When I went down to get them, they hauled them 25 miles

02:08:45.354 --> 02:08:50.057
away to Pleasant Grove and they charged me $711

02:08:50.121 --> 02:08:53.842
for each one of them for

02:08:53.971 --> 02:08:57.499
one day. And that's a huge

02:08:58.493 --> 02:09:02.337
amount of money out of my pocket for somebody who's just starting

02:09:02.353 --> 02:09:05.502
over. I just moved out here, got my mother

02:09:06.002 --> 02:09:09.054
living with me and a son, and, uh,

02:09:09.761 --> 02:09:12.975
wow, it's, uh, you know, I've looked

02:09:13.475 --> 02:09:16.285
into this, I've done some research on it, and, uh,

02:09:17.072 --> 02:09:20.325
there's not much I can do. I understand that, and I, I understand

02:09:20.825 --> 02:09:24.282
there's codes and that they have to be enforced, but I would just

02:09:24.396 --> 02:09:29.455
suggest maybe that— one

02:09:29.504 --> 02:09:32.414
time before when I lived down in Highland, there was, you know, I got a

02:09:32.494 --> 02:09:35.831
notice for a trailer being on the road. They came and knocked on my door

02:09:35.879 --> 02:09:38.955
and asked me, you know, told me there was a code. They left a notice

02:09:39.084 --> 02:09:42.791
on my door. But they left the tags on my trailer.

02:09:43.212 --> 02:09:46.597
I didn't even see them because I got home after 6 o'clock. It's dark.

02:09:47.164 --> 02:09:51.101
And Monday they were gone before I even got home. So I'm

02:09:51.198 --> 02:09:54.402
just saying that it might be maybe the length of time,

02:09:55.159 --> 02:09:58.460
you know, like maybe 10 days or something, give somebody some

02:09:58.960 --> 02:10:02.386
time so that they are out of town or whatever, that they have some time

02:10:02.418 --> 02:10:04.607
that they can move them. I certainly would have moved them,

02:10:06.066 --> 02:10:09.247
but to come home to, you know, a $1,400 bill,

02:10:10.109 --> 02:10:13.770
it's tough. 30 seconds remaining. That's all I

02:10:14.270 --> 02:10:14.909
had to say. Thank you.

02:10:18.698 --> 02:10:19.308
Charlotte Dukos.

02:10:22.086 --> 02:10:24.637
Hello, Charlotte Dukos.

02:10:25.300 --> 02:10:28.206
Um, I am here actually to speak with about something that is not on the

02:10:28.706 --> 02:10:32.578
agenda but, um, is an item for the community. I am the student

02:10:33.078 --> 02:10:36.983
council advisor at Cedar Valley High School, and on December 4th from 5 to 10

02:10:37.015 --> 02:10:40.120
PM, would like to invite the community to

02:10:40.364 --> 02:10:43.634
Cedar Valley High School for Christmas in the Valley. It is a program where we

02:10:44.134 --> 02:10:47.423
are raising money for people in our community to

02:10:47.923 --> 02:10:51.261
help them out at Christmas time. And we have all kinds of fun activities

02:10:51.437 --> 02:10:54.584
for families. There's live entertainment, we'll have food,

02:10:54.649 --> 02:10:57.764
there's a kids carnival and things like that.

02:10:58.582 --> 02:11:01.296
And everything that's raised will go back into the community.

02:11:01.954 --> 02:11:05.390
But it also will— we'll have some services there. There will be a free clothing

02:11:05.503 --> 02:11:09.211
swap, so you can bring clothes and get clothes. Free toy swaps.

02:11:09.259 --> 02:11:12.805
You can bring toys or get toys, which is a great time at Christmas

02:11:13.305 --> 02:11:17.088
time to do that. There will be some service opportunities there as well. And,

02:11:17.537 --> 02:11:20.682
and we just want to invite the community. So I came here to make that

02:11:21.182 --> 02:11:25.174
announcement here tonight because hopefully there's a few people listening. And I've left some

02:11:25.238 --> 02:11:28.527
flyers with Lacey as well if the city is willing to put

02:11:29.027 --> 02:11:32.281
those up in their offices. But it's, it's a full community event

02:11:32.781 --> 02:11:36.037
and we hope that people will come out and get the things they need and

02:11:36.537 --> 02:11:39.707
give the things they can and, and, and make this

02:11:39.756 --> 02:11:43.377
something that we can be a benefit to our community. So thanks for the

02:11:43.877 --> 02:11:45.253
opportunity to speak about that for a minute.

02:11:48.950 --> 02:11:52.512
That is all. Okay, perfect. Is there anyone else

02:11:53.012 --> 02:11:56.915
here that did not get an opportunity to speak? Seeing no one, at 7:20

02:11:57.590 --> 02:12:00.798
we'll close the public comment period and bring it back to the council for,

02:12:01.039 --> 02:12:04.767
uh, comments, and I'm going to start with Council Member Clark. Thanks,

02:12:04.831 --> 02:12:07.724
Mayor. Sorry, I was just putting— giving myself a note,

02:12:07.820 --> 02:12:11.869
um, to remind myself to print the flyers that

02:12:11.966 --> 02:12:15.662
Charlotte has and hang them up around our area of town too.

02:12:16.144 --> 02:12:20.177
Um, I, I look forward to what

02:12:20.241 --> 02:12:23.696
the Cedar Valley High School is going to put on. Um, we also have Eagle

02:12:24.196 --> 02:12:27.904
Mountain residents that attend Westlake And they're also doing something too.

02:12:27.953 --> 02:12:31.629
So, and they're on completely different nights, so you can go and support both.

02:12:32.705 --> 02:12:36.382
But we're— I'm really grateful for the things that members

02:12:36.882 --> 02:12:40.444
of our community do this time of year. That is one of the best

02:12:40.492 --> 02:12:44.105
things about Eco Mountain is that we look out for each other and we take

02:12:44.605 --> 02:12:48.151
care of one another when times got tough. And I was thinking when

02:12:48.280 --> 02:12:51.651
Mr. Hunsaker was speaking, I was like, man, we need to do like a GoFundMe

02:12:52.151 --> 02:12:55.625
or or something to help because it's just,

02:12:55.754 --> 02:12:58.968
it's a rough situation and I totally understand how hard that was.

02:12:59.065 --> 02:13:00.971
And thank you for sharing your experience with us.

02:13:03.030 --> 02:13:06.338
I'm really excited for what we get to do tonight.

02:13:07.779 --> 02:13:11.450
Todd Black was a really special part of our team,

02:13:12.481 --> 02:13:16.329
sorry, at the city. Aw. And I think

02:13:16.829 --> 02:13:20.483
we all loved him. We loved his candor, we loved how blunt he

02:13:20.983 --> 02:13:24.497
was, and we love how fiercely protective

02:13:24.997 --> 02:13:28.688
he was of Eagle Mountain and the special things that make us Eagle

02:13:29.188 --> 02:13:33.938
Mountain. So I'm really excited and I'm grateful to those

02:13:34.034 --> 02:13:37.182
who've put the money forward so that we can have the

02:13:37.682 --> 02:13:41.597
scholarship program in his name, because it's going to be a really cool

02:13:48.649 --> 02:13:50.566
I can just say ditto and be done, but I won't.

02:13:51.919 --> 02:13:55.391
I should probably. I mean,

02:13:55.424 --> 02:13:58.886
I just, I wasn't able to be to the Veterans Breakfast, and so I just

02:13:59.386 --> 02:14:01.506
want to wish the vets a happy Vets Day. A little bit late for me.

02:14:01.571 --> 02:14:04.612
We were out of town, my wife and I, and I was thinking about them,

02:14:05.034 --> 02:14:08.597
and I'm just grateful for their service and all of our,

02:14:08.840 --> 02:14:11.024
all of our our service professionals,

02:14:12.163 --> 02:14:16.077
fire and police and those that run into harm's way rather

02:14:16.109 --> 02:14:19.719
than away from it. Thanksgiving is coming up.

02:14:19.895 --> 02:14:23.360
I just want to remind us all to think

02:14:23.408 --> 02:14:26.681
broadly, look outside of your own box, look outside of perhaps your

02:14:27.181 --> 02:14:29.472
own family and invite someone who might be alone,

02:14:30.531 --> 02:14:33.611
a couple who might be new, or— you're invited to my house, Mr.

02:14:33.723 --> 02:14:36.049
Hunsaker. If you want to come to my house for Thanksgiving, you're invited. Thank you.

02:14:36.163 --> 02:14:39.823
Someone new to the community. I just,

02:14:40.356 --> 02:14:43.680
I think it's important that we look after and care for one another. And if

02:14:44.180 --> 02:14:46.423
you'll stick around to the end of the meeting or just leave a phone number

02:14:46.923 --> 02:14:49.021
where we can get a hold of you, I would like to have a conversation

02:14:49.521 --> 02:14:53.610
with you, if I may. So if you'd leave that with somebody in

02:14:53.643 --> 02:14:56.372
the back, perhaps, I just ask you to do that.

02:14:58.964 --> 02:15:02.841
Anyway, I just, I'm really grateful for this time of year. I'm grateful to

02:15:03.443 --> 02:15:07.449
be thinking about Thanksgiving. Thanksgiving and just the blessing that Thanksgiving

02:15:07.481 --> 02:15:10.946
is. I have 4 beautiful children. They're all healthy

02:15:11.446 --> 02:15:14.849
and sound and well. I have 9 grandchildren, and they're all healthy and well.

02:15:16.282 --> 02:15:19.409
I have a wife that's put up with me for 39 years. That's just the

02:15:19.441 --> 02:15:23.355
start of my blessings. I hope that

02:15:23.855 --> 02:15:28.721
we can look inside and just realize— excuse me— just

02:15:28.769 --> 02:15:32.326
realize the blessings that we enjoy as neighbors, friends,

02:15:32.795 --> 02:15:36.878
and community members in the best city, in the best

02:15:37.378 --> 02:15:38.566
state, in the nation. Thank you.

02:15:43.104 --> 02:15:46.339
Thanks for coming. I always love to see people here. I don't know who this

02:15:46.839 --> 02:15:49.105
young group that just came in here— welcome, thanks for coming tonight.

02:15:50.010 --> 02:15:53.810
Hopefully you get some benefit from being here and seeing

02:15:53.826 --> 02:15:57.530
how things work in a city. I've been thinking a lot about Thanksgiving

02:15:58.067 --> 02:16:01.982
coming up next week, and I feel a little bit like

02:16:02.482 --> 02:16:06.093
a family that's had a quarrel, to be honest with you. Uh,

02:16:06.109 --> 02:16:09.774
with the tax, uh, discussion this year, we've done a lot of

02:16:09.806 --> 02:16:12.907
bickering internally as a city,

02:16:13.245 --> 02:16:15.000
as citizens, city council.

02:16:16.062 --> 02:16:18.494
Um, and I,

02:16:19.685 --> 02:16:23.279
I will be praying for peace this next week in our

02:16:23.779 --> 02:16:30.714
city. I think that we are— it's

02:16:31.214 --> 02:16:31.891
a community I care about.

02:16:38.743 --> 02:16:42.359
And I want you to know, first of all, just from my— from me,

02:16:43.404 --> 02:16:46.506
the things that have been said on social media about the people who are sitting

02:16:46.538 --> 02:16:50.118
up here are just untrue. And it's a little disheartening to see see

02:16:50.618 --> 02:16:52.719
some of the things that have been said that are just absolute lies.

02:16:54.116 --> 02:16:58.612
The people up here that are sitting on this council and our mayor are

02:16:59.112 --> 02:17:02.257
some of the, the best people that I know. They have integrity

02:17:02.787 --> 02:17:06.528
and they have acted with integrity. And it's not easy making decisions

02:17:06.544 --> 02:17:09.932
that cause taxes to go up.

02:17:10.574 --> 02:17:14.363
And I can tell you those decisions were never made lightly. We pay them

02:17:14.428 --> 02:17:16.355
as well. And I,

02:17:18.416 --> 02:17:21.679
for what it's worth, we made the decision because

02:17:22.179 --> 02:17:24.081
we felt like it was the best decision for the future of our city.

02:17:25.016 --> 02:17:27.968
So in this next few months,

02:17:28.146 --> 02:17:31.953
as we maybe reflect on the things we're

02:17:32.453 --> 02:17:35.792
thankful for, how we can be better people to each other, I hope that we

02:17:36.292 --> 02:17:40.019
will try to mend fences. We'll find ways forward, even in disagreement.

02:17:40.761 --> 02:17:43.583
Thank you. Thank you for being here. Thank you for being engaged.

02:17:45.349 --> 02:17:49.030
Uh, I love being in Eagle Mountain. Uh, I make a choice to be here

02:17:49.530 --> 02:17:52.673
every day and to stay here, and I hope you will too. Thanks.

02:17:56.563 --> 02:18:00.081
Thank you to my fellow council members and for all of you for

02:18:00.581 --> 02:18:03.341
showing up tonight. Um, grateful for you.

02:18:05.272 --> 02:18:09.336
And, uh, Greg, I Spoke with Greg Hunsaker earlier this week

02:18:09.836 --> 02:18:12.557
or last week, and he shared the story with me, and I thought, that's,

02:18:12.685 --> 02:18:16.370
that's not the Eagle Mountain way to welcome someone who just

02:18:16.870 --> 02:18:20.248
went down with— my daughter was actually part of the band that he was probably

02:18:20.312 --> 02:18:23.838
escorting or hauling her drum, uh, to St. George. And, and I

02:18:24.338 --> 02:18:28.485
don't know, Mayor, if it's appropriate, maybe in a future work session we can review

02:18:28.985 --> 02:18:32.747
the policy as it's applied. Sometimes things get passed.

02:18:33.215 --> 02:18:37.241
with a certain intent in mind, but those types of outcomes maybe aren't

02:18:37.322 --> 02:18:39.844
what we have intentioned. I'd just love to better understand,

02:18:40.878 --> 02:18:45.082
uh, the code that exists that led, led to that specific example, and maybe

02:18:45.582 --> 02:18:48.151
better understand, um,

02:18:48.938 --> 02:18:52.554
why we're impounding vehicles to Linden. That might be a sheriff's office

02:18:53.054 --> 02:18:56.432
thing. I'm not sure how that all kind of transpires, but I'd love just some

02:18:56.932 --> 02:19:01.238
education from the council standpoint how we can better direct that.

02:19:01.595 --> 02:19:05.130
Um, I understand why the code exists, but I'd love to sharpen it and fine-tune

02:19:05.630 --> 02:19:09.201
it if we can make that better. Thank you for sharing your experience. I wanted

02:19:09.701 --> 02:19:13.266
to just share, um, a personal experience,

02:19:13.314 --> 02:19:16.112
and I'll try not to get emotional. Um,

02:19:17.048 --> 02:19:21.339
a couple days ago, there was a, a mom that reached out on

02:19:21.371 --> 02:19:25.081
the citizens page, and, uh, she, she was asking if there

02:19:25.581 --> 02:19:29.641
was anyone in the community that that has a Cybertruck for

02:19:30.141 --> 02:19:32.505
her little boy to go for a ride. He has cancer.

02:19:33.755 --> 02:19:37.096
And it brought back a flood

02:19:37.596 --> 02:19:41.164
of memories for me personally when our daughter went through this in Eagle Mountain.

02:19:41.422 --> 02:19:44.936
We had a city that stepped up at the time. The Miss

02:19:44.968 --> 02:19:49.396
Eagle Mountain and the mayor, Heather Jackson, at the time, they had

02:19:49.896 --> 02:19:52.883
a limo pull up to our house. They had Disney princesses come into our home

02:19:52.936 --> 02:19:56.378
and took her out to breakfast. It was a really big

02:19:56.394 --> 02:20:00.663
deal. They even put placemats with our daughter's

02:20:00.680 --> 02:20:02.669
picture on it, and it was just a really cool experience.

02:20:04.097 --> 02:20:05.836
And it brought back a flood of emotions.

02:20:07.746 --> 02:20:11.393
And our community has stepped

02:20:11.893 --> 02:20:15.364
up. They're doing a car show for this little boy now on Saturday morning— or

02:20:15.864 --> 02:20:19.016
Sunday, excuse me, not Saturday, it's Sunday. So I'm going to have to miss church.

02:20:19.835 --> 02:20:23.499
But that's okay to go to a car show for this little guy. But they're

02:20:23.999 --> 02:20:27.147
trying to raise funds. And I just think it's really cool.

02:20:27.356 --> 02:20:30.128
The mom asked for a ride in a Cybertruck, and now they're doing a car

02:20:30.193 --> 02:20:33.894
show for this little kid. And that is what

02:20:34.394 --> 02:20:39.023
I hope when people move to Eagle Mountain, that's the kind of community that

02:20:39.315 --> 02:20:43.705
we want them to feel and participate in. So I'm grateful.

02:20:43.997 --> 02:20:47.654
Thank you. For our community. I'm grateful for the residents, even the

02:20:47.670 --> 02:20:50.729
hard conversations that we've had.

02:20:50.874 --> 02:20:53.578
I know I've had more than I can count.

02:20:54.287 --> 02:20:57.883
I'm grateful for them because it sharpens me. It makes me think more deeply

02:20:57.900 --> 02:21:01.302
about the decisions that are made here and

02:21:01.708 --> 02:21:03.388
just express my gratitude. Thank you.

02:21:05.744 --> 02:21:09.165
All right, thank you. I just,

02:21:09.779 --> 02:21:13.193
again, I could just say ditto too. A couple quick things. One thing,

02:21:13.942 --> 02:21:17.406
I love Veterans Day and I love our veterans and our men and women who

02:21:17.790 --> 02:21:21.318
put a badge on every day and do what they do for the rest

02:21:21.818 --> 02:21:25.343
of us. One thing that I've done for almost 15 years

02:21:25.843 --> 02:21:29.112
is take a disabled vet on a cow elk

02:21:29.612 --> 02:21:32.752
hunt. Part of my profession before I got to do this was guide

02:21:32.784 --> 02:21:36.039
big game hunts and I did that again this year. It's just over the

02:21:36.055 --> 02:21:39.246
weekend, a couple of days,

02:21:39.278 --> 02:21:42.923
and we go out and hunt an elk. I've done it twice with Adam

02:21:42.971 --> 02:21:46.939
Ekel, Outdoors KSL. So this year it will be aired on KSL

02:21:46.987 --> 02:21:50.265
again. But Adam interviewed him after he'd

02:21:50.765 --> 02:21:55.470
harvested an elk, and he just broke down and told why he chose

02:21:55.503 --> 02:21:58.507
to serve. And so very impactful,

02:21:58.941 --> 02:22:02.652
and I love that kind of stuff. So I'm just

02:22:03.152 --> 02:22:04.693
glad to be a part of that and be able to give back to our

02:22:04.741 --> 02:22:08.131
vets. And we appreciate all those who put their

02:22:08.179 --> 02:22:11.344
lives on the line for whatever it is they do. Also, uh,

02:22:12.357 --> 02:22:14.638
the something that we're going to get to do here in a minute that I'm

02:22:14.703 --> 02:22:18.880
pretty excited about— I don't think there's anyone that would

02:22:19.025 --> 02:22:22.110
argue or push back on Todd as much

02:22:22.610 --> 02:22:25.854
as me, but I also know that he would jump in my truck and say,

02:22:25.934 --> 02:22:29.485
we're going to the meeting together. And we kind of had a special little bond.

02:22:29.550 --> 02:22:32.667
And I know a time when Councilman Wright and I went and planted trees

02:22:32.683 --> 02:22:36.346
with him for of the afternoon. And, you know, he's just a special guy

02:22:36.394 --> 02:22:39.704
that, uh, he didn't question where

02:22:39.753 --> 02:22:43.014
you were at with God. He kind of knew. So, uh,

02:22:43.384 --> 02:22:47.144
but we loved having him in our city, and, uh, I enjoyed

02:22:47.644 --> 02:22:50.454
our relationship. It was actually pretty special. So,

02:22:51.241 --> 02:22:54.020
uh, just grateful that his family could come and join us with, uh,

02:22:55.033 --> 02:22:59.050
in celebrating some of his accomplishments. So with

02:22:59.550 --> 02:23:02.753
that, Um, we can move on first to our consent

02:23:03.253 --> 02:23:07.384
agenda, and I know 13A has been

02:23:07.884 --> 02:23:11.358
asked to be removed. Mayor, I'll make a motion if you'll take it. Go ahead.

02:23:11.630 --> 02:23:15.012
Move that we approve the consent agenda removing item 13A

02:23:15.512 --> 02:23:17.560
and placing it on our regularly scheduled agenda.

02:23:18.858 --> 02:23:22.207
Second. Okay, we have a motion by Council Member Wright and a second

02:23:22.707 --> 02:23:26.010
by Council Member Wood. And Council Member Clark? Yes. Councilmember Wright?

