02:53:22.643 --> 02:53:26.061
kind of give you a little bit of history on this, Council,

02:53:26.077 --> 02:53:29.401
you'll remember that we've talked a couple times about the

02:53:29.513 --> 02:53:33.174
issue of transmission lines in the Ag Zone

02:53:33.928 --> 02:53:38.203
back in 2024. There was an amendment

02:53:38.703 --> 02:53:43.959
made to the allowed land uses in

02:53:43.991 --> 02:53:47.692
the agricultural zone, and public

02:53:47.757 --> 02:53:51.588
and private utility— public

02:53:52.088 --> 02:53:56.502
and private utilities as a use was just stricken from

02:53:57.002 --> 02:54:00.679
that zone. So the issue we run into, obviously, is we have

02:54:01.562 --> 02:54:05.547
data centers, uh, we have particularly the, the Meta

02:54:05.563 --> 02:54:08.985
data center, um, has, uh,

02:54:10.238 --> 02:54:13.693
was, uh, there's a transmission

02:54:14.193 --> 02:54:17.180
line coming from Spanish Fork to the Mercer substation,

02:54:17.613 --> 02:54:20.747
and the— in

02:54:21.247 --> 02:54:24.249
that alignment, and I'll, I'll bring you back to that here,

02:54:25.245 --> 02:54:28.560
you can see the alignment that that runs on the

02:54:28.625 --> 02:54:32.275
backside of the lake mountains. It's supposed to run right to the data

02:54:32.775 --> 02:54:36.458
center. And so that alignment takes it right through our ag

02:54:36.958 --> 02:54:41.199
zones, our ag zone. And so with the

02:54:43.189 --> 02:54:46.484
ability taken to allow transmission

02:54:46.984 --> 02:54:50.609
lines in that zone, we have had Rocky Mountain Power

02:54:51.109 --> 02:54:53.798
contact us and ask, well, what's our— What's your position?

02:54:55.927 --> 02:54:59.452
How do we get power to the substation

02:54:59.484 --> 02:55:03.505
there, the Mercer substation? So you asked

02:55:03.570 --> 02:55:06.851
us to explore looking into an overlay zone. We did

02:55:06.948 --> 02:55:10.488
that. We met with Spanish Fork City because

02:55:10.585 --> 02:55:12.803
they were another city that had a similar circumstance.

02:55:14.642 --> 02:55:20.121
What we learned from them was that they had decided

02:55:20.170 --> 02:55:23.857
not to use an overlay zone. They became more aware of some

02:55:23.905 --> 02:55:29.025
state code provisions, and I brought

02:55:29.525 --> 02:55:33.023
that back to you, and we decided that maybe overlay zone wasn't the right

02:55:33.523 --> 02:55:37.087
tool to allow transmission— to permit transmission

02:55:37.135 --> 02:55:40.663
lines through the ag zone. So what our proposal is,

02:55:40.760 --> 02:55:44.191
is to come back and just simply allow

02:55:44.256 --> 02:55:48.007
them as a special use in in that,

02:55:48.331 --> 02:55:51.422
in the agricultural zone. Along with that,

02:55:53.720 --> 02:55:57.306
we, with utility public

02:55:57.806 --> 02:56:02.475
and private being, with public and private utilities being kind

02:56:02.975 --> 02:56:06.622
of stricken as a permitted use, that if you look at the definition of utilities,

02:56:07.040 --> 02:56:11.180
that eliminates like culinary water lines, power lines,

02:56:11.555 --> 02:56:15.311
sewer lines. And so I think it might be wise to

02:56:16.340 --> 02:56:19.654
put those— put utilities back in as an allowed

02:56:19.719 --> 02:56:23.116
use in the Ag Zone and then allow trans— as a

02:56:23.616 --> 02:56:26.662
special use and power transmission lines

02:56:27.162 --> 02:56:31.594
as a special use. And the reason why they're special is because in Chapter

02:56:32.094 --> 02:56:36.044
1775, there are special requirements

02:56:36.896 --> 02:56:40.876
that relate to these uses. And so if we

02:56:41.085 --> 02:56:45.412
make them special uses, particularly for public and private utilities,

02:56:45.913 --> 02:56:49.904
we get to benefit from the additional requirements in 1775

02:56:49.952 --> 02:56:54.355
that relate to ground-mounted

02:56:54.403 --> 02:56:58.581
utility boxes. There's some landscape and location requirements

02:56:58.630 --> 02:57:02.407
that we benefit from by having those tied

02:57:02.439 --> 02:57:06.554
to the special use— as a special use. Transmission lines,

02:57:07.613 --> 02:57:11.419
there's a reference to transmission lines in that special chapter,

02:57:11.563 --> 02:57:14.775
but it really, all it does is just ties back

02:57:15.275 --> 02:57:19.094
to our Title 13 requirements, which are related to

02:57:19.287 --> 02:57:22.610
installation of utilities, which it would have been tied to anyway. So there's really

02:57:23.124 --> 02:57:26.849
not much of a, there's minimal

02:57:26.962 --> 02:57:30.703
benefit, I guess, of it being a special use. But that's our proposal.

02:57:32.182 --> 02:57:36.323
staff's proposal to you that we allow utilities

02:57:36.436 --> 02:57:40.515
again as a standalone use in the ag zone and allow transmission

02:57:40.612 --> 02:57:43.764
lines so it can get over to the Mercer substation.

02:57:43.878 --> 02:57:47.522
So I'm here with any questions to answer, any questions you might

02:57:48.022 --> 02:57:51.324
have. I don't know if this is a good question, but it's a question I

02:57:51.340 --> 02:57:54.634
have in my mind. If a property owner that

02:57:54.650 --> 02:57:57.919
is in the ag zone wants to Let's say put up a cell tower

02:57:58.915 --> 02:58:02.529
for public or private use, would this allow them to do that?

02:58:03.846 --> 02:58:07.059
My understanding is we permit

02:58:07.559 --> 02:58:11.058
cell towers differently. So if you

02:58:11.558 --> 02:58:14.961
look on the table there, you see communication facilities and towers is already

02:58:14.977 --> 02:58:17.997
a special use. Yeah. So this wouldn't change that.

02:58:18.447 --> 02:58:22.205
Exactly. There's a, in 1775,

02:58:22.630 --> 02:58:28.323
There is a specific— there's a set of specific standards for communication

02:58:28.823 --> 02:58:32.674
facilities and cell towers. So this

02:58:32.738 --> 02:58:36.175
wouldn't affect that. So I've got a question about

02:58:36.675 --> 02:58:39.980
the use of the word facilities. Do we want to be more

02:58:40.480 --> 02:58:45.230
specific about that? Because that could have a very broad generalization

